 "titulo": {
  "estudio": "«Chi» y «quanto» relativos",
  "alumno": "Interpreting relatives without an explicit antecedent"
 },
 "intro": "Double or mixed relative pronouns pack the demonstrative antecedent and the relative pronoun into a single word: **chi** equals «colui che / colei che / coloro che» (whoever, those who, the one who) and refers only to people in the singular; while **quanto** equals «tutto ciò che / quello che» (all that, everything that) and refers to neuter things or overall quantities.",
